# P1-007B offline policy counterfactuals

Read-only replay of four verified P1-006 cARL/JEV responses. No model inference was used.

| Case | Actual cARL | Strict arbiter | Review all sensitive | Direction-aware triage |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| public_access_regression | review_required | review_required | review_required | review_required |
| public_access_remediation | review_required | review_required | review_required | expedited_human_review |
| ssh_world_open | review_required | review_required | review_required | review_required |
| ssh_scope_remediation | review_required | review_required | review_required | expedited_human_review |

**Policy meaning:** `direction_aware_triage` does NOT grant approval. It assigns an experimental `expedited_human_review` queue when low control-reduction and scope-expansion signals coexist with a security-sensitive change. It is intentionally not a deployable control.

**Important limitation:** Low reduction/expansion scores do not prove a remediation is effective or safe. This variant uses only score patterns, not independent ground truth, and can misclassify other changes.

